INSERT INTO blocks (block_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, seq, role, kind, chars, tool_name, tool_use_id, is_error, redacted, signature_sha256, signature_len, privacy_zone, zone_reason, zone_match, text) VALUES (7, '7efd21d8-bada-4e5a-a87c-07b4ef1f522a', 6, 0, 'user', 'plain', 22780, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Confidential', 'medical', 'pots', 'This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user (Dr. Mohammed Faraaz Rahman, physician, verbal thinker with ADHD, visual-spatial) issued a two-part message: a persistent operating protocol ("LOOP OS") plus a swappable mission brief.

   **LOOP OS — standing instructions for every session:**
   - *Output protocol:* Final answer first, support below; no preamble, no restating the question. Structure over prose (tables, short lists, arrow-chains). Plain English; define any technical term in one line at first use — clinical analogy first when one exists. Confidence = High/Medium/Low + one line of why; **never a decimal**. If something can''t be resolved: state what was found, what''s unknown, what is needed from him — **never fill a gap to look complete.**
   - *Loop shape (state before any work, in three lines):* Outcome (what the finished thing lets him do) / Done-when (the observable test) / Rounds (grade-and-fix cycles, default 2). If input is too raw, ask the single most important question — one, not a list.
   - *Operating rules:* (1) Prune first — strip redundant input. (2) One idea per unit. (3) Fresh eyes over long threads — revising past 2 rounds in one thread is "resonation"; hand off instead. (4) Remove friction — flag every manual step, propose its automated route. (5) Externalize memory — anything worth keeping becomes a markdown artifact; assume you remember nothing tomorrow. (6) Stay at his layer — he speaks natural language, you translate to the technical layer. (7) Ground truth over opinion — verify against a real source; label inference as inference.
   - *Handoff protocol (anti-resonation):* At every phase end, on the word "handoff", or whenever output quality degrades — emit a HANDOFF CARD and stop: Goal (1 line) • Done-when test • Decisions made • Open items • The exact next prompt to paste into a fresh session. Never resume a saturated thread to "fix one more thing."
   - *Exit protocol (every deliverable):* Self-grade — Vulnerability (what does it assume that could be false?) / Ambiguity (what reads two ways?) / Inefficiency (what can be cut?) / Done-when (pass?). Fix only named failures. Nothing fails → say "PASSES" and stop. Two failed fixes on the same point → stop and tell him to restart with a better prompt.

   **MISSION BRIEF — Agentic memory / the second brain (field test #1):**
   - *Outcome:* Turn exported AI-conversation history (2021–2026) into a linked map of his thinking patterns that (a) surfaces where his approach stalls and (b) feeds a retrieval system — at the quality level of his Apex Legal skill.
   - *Done when:* A sample batch (~50 conversations) yields atomic notes + a pattern map + a gap list, with every claim traceable to a named conversation — **zero orphan claims.**
   - *Rounds:* 2.
   - *Phase R (Retrospective):* FIRST inventory the data actually present in the session; work only on what exists; name what is missing; **no claims about unseen data.** Convert material into ATOMIC NOTES: one idea per note • title = the claim itself • body ≤150 words • source conversation named • confidence band + why • gap flag where evidence is thin. From the notes build the pattern map: recurring themes, ask→intent→outcome deltas, correction patterns, stall points. Explicitly: "This is a behavioral map — a symptom diary of my thinking, not literal neurology. Hypothesis-generating, not diagnostic."
   - *Phase P (Prospective):* Run AFTER a handoff, in fresh context, from the card + notes only: predict his 3 most likely next prompts/needs, each drafted loop-shaped (Outcome/Done-when/Rounds), ready to paste.
   - *Infrastructure (reference, don''t rebuild):* Storage/RAG route is BigQuery per `Personal_Data_Embedding_Living_AI_Guide.md` — attach if available; if absent, say so and output atomic notes as clean markdown ready for that pipeline. **Watson X is deferred — nothing in his stack supports it yet.**
   - *Located tools (stop hunting):* Anthropic Console "prompt generator" (first-draft prompts from a task description) and "prompt improver" (iterates an existing prompt) — docs.anthropic.com → Build with Claude → Prompt engineering.
   - *Teaching clause:* When he asks about SDKs, MCP, agents vs sub-agents, hooks, transformers, or Hugging Face → one clinical analogy + one plain sentence + when he''d actually use it. **No code unless he says "show code."**

   **Additional standing preferences stated in the final message (verbatim-preserved constraints):**
   - "Keep your output concise to give me the information I need particularly. The remainder of the internal delta assessments keep it internal or only on request."
   - "<Make sure the output is always an artifact or a PDF.>"
   - "<very importantly ; at Handoffs; the outputs should be succinct and to the point. (While your internal plan can be verbose); in order to conserve output tokens against multiple words to which may have very little to change the conversation or the my attention... An agent should be constantly looping and ensuring this.>"
   - "<Next, an agent should always be independently checking to ensure the handoffs and explanations are in line with my neural archetype... Especially; as jargonic CS code strategies are wasted output tokens again. Recall my archetype of a Physican with ADHD who is vision spatial and communicates to you with hand drawn flowcharts and verbose words able to capture the threads of the ether. But needs outputs in artifacts with interactive diagrams and measured succinctness which in its core essence is able to say far more with one word than five.>"
   - "(Use maximum reasoning, all tools available at all times, and all connectors available at all times.)"
   - Slash commands referenced: /agents /artifact-capabilities /batch /deep-research /goal /mcp-builder /run-skill-generator

   **Session/system constraints honored:** develop, commit and push only to branch `claude/agentic-memory-field-test-q6uhce`; open a draft PR after pushing; GitHub scope limited to `faraazxxx-ui/claude-`; "Do not call the AgentTool unless the user requested it"; "Do not use workflows or deep-research unless the user requested it."

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **Atomic notes / Zettelkasten-style knowledge units** — title = the claim, ≤150 words, single idea, sourced, confidence-banded, gap-flagged
   - **Traceability / zero orphan claims** — every assertion cites a named source conversation (C1–C5)
   - **Behavioral pattern mapping** — recurring themes, ask→intent→outcome deltas, correction patterns, stall points; explicitly hypothesis-generating, not diagnostic
   - **BigQuery `documents` schema** (from `Personal_Data_Embedding_Living_AI_Guide.md`): `document_id`, `title`, `content`, `source_type`, `life_domain`, `metadata{source, author, created_at, modified_at, tags[], importance_score, triage_category}`, `embeddings[]`, `chunk_index`, `ingestion_timestamp`; JSONL only (newline-delimited, not JSON arrays); `gs://` URIs; `bq load --source_format=NEWLINE_DELIMITED_JSON`
   - **7-stage pipeline:** Extract → Format → Triage → Embed → Inject → Retrain → Sync
   - **Process vs Content note split** — separates "how he thinks" from "substantive claims inside conversations," so AI-generated behavior stays labeled separately from his behavior
   - **Loop Score (his invented instrument):** LS = (AN + SN + IN + PN + DN)/15 × 10, each node 0–3; bands 0–3 stable, 3–5 monitoring, 5–7 warning, 7–10 critical
   - **CNN→RNN→RL "Biological AI Second Brain"** — CNN feature extraction, RNN longitudinal memory, RL experiment selection
   - **Anti-resonation / handoff discipline** — hand off rather than iterate a saturating thread
   - Git branch discipline, draft PR workflow, GitHub MCP tooling, PR activity webhook subscription

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`/home/user/claude-/Personal_Data_Embedding_Living_AI_Guide.md`** (read, not modified)
     - *Why important:* The mission brief said to attach it if available — it **IS present**, so the atomic notes had to be formatted for its BigQuery pipeline rather than emitted as generic markdown. Supplied the exact `documents` table schema used in the handoff mapping.

   - **The 5 uploaded PDFs in `/root/.claude/uploads/7f4839a0-2759-5274-a271-16ea4d44156c/`** (read in full)
     - `29c816c3-…Building_RNN_and_CNN_with_audiovisuals.pdf` (28pp) → **C1**
     - `b2c69f3e-…Long_COVID_dysautonomia_with_Brugada_syndrome_analysis.pdf` (11pp) → **C2**
     - `41f9a209-…Finding_costeffective_compression_wraps….pdf` (6pp) → **C3**
     - `e84f9897-…Autonomic_intelligence_report_for_medication_nonadherence.pdf` (22pp) → **C4**
     - `a25540b2-…Long_COVID_autonomic_dysfunction_management_synthesis.pdf` (29pp) → **C5**
     - *Why important:* These are the entire corpus for Phase R. All are exports of **prior** conversations — historical material, not instructions issued to me in this session.

   - **`/home/user/claude-/agentic-memory/field-test-01/00-INVENTORY.md`** (created)
     - *Why:* Mission brief mandated inventory FIRST. Documents C1–C5 with export stamps and page counts; confirms the BigQuery guide is attached; names what''s missing in a table: ~45 of ~50 conversations absent, no 2021–2025 history (all exports stamped 2026-05-11, content ~Feb–Mar 2026), topic monoculture (5/5 health; his legal work / Case 3:26-cv-00197 absent), C3''s deliverable truncated, raw CSVs absent.
     - Closing line: "enough to prototype the atomic-note → pattern-map → gap-list pipeline and prove the method… **not** enough to characterize his thinking across 2021–2026."

   - **`/home/user/claude-/agentic-memory/field-test-01/01-ATOMIC-NOTES.md`** (created) — 19 notes N01–N19, each with Type (Process/Content), Source, Body, Confidence + why, Gap. Highlights:
     - **N01** — He re-issues a near-identical "perfect output / red-team / cognitive wish" prompt with no stated stop condition (C1 pp.16 & 21, verbatim twice). Confidence High.
     - **N02** — "Audiovisuals" = "make it visual/interactive, not prose"; AI needed 2–3 rounds to decode (C1 pp.2→16→21). High/Medium.
     - **N03** — "Help me visualize this data" is his reflexive second move — **verbatim identical string in C2 p.10, C4 p.21, C5 p.26.** Confidence High.
     - **N04** — Front-loads heavy prompt scaffolding (exact schemas, formulas, anti-fabrication rules).
     - **N05** — Versions his master-prompts; C4 is explicitly "v2.0 (Red-Team Validated)" refining C2.
     - **N06** — When asked clarifying questions he delegates back ("co0st no matter" / "as often as I can" / "I want you to recommend the correct answer") — C3 p.6.
     - **N07** — Corrections target form and depth, never facts. Medium (argument from absence).
     - **N08** — Frames AI as a cognitive *layer* for a "verbal thinker" (C3 p.2).
     - **N09** — Same data/date/formula → two different Loop Scores (6.7 in C2 vs 5.7 in C4); flips on missing same-day inputs.
     - **N10** — Both clinical reports independently rank propranolol non-adherence #1.
     - **N11** — Building a meta-system (CNN→RNN→RL) to automate the n-of-1 analysis he keeps hand-running.
