INSERT INTO blocks (block_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, seq, role, kind, chars, tool_name, tool_use_id, is_error, redacted, signature_sha256, signature_len, privacy_zone, zone_reason, zone_match, text) VALUES (65, 'e111ba91-96cf-415e-a486-153752dfad07', 50, 0, 'assistant', 'text', 1476, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Private work', 'session-internal', '', '**Artifact:** https://claude.ai/code/artifact/2a2b2fe6-6cff-4d64-a871-c6aaaf3a9550

Phase R is now the thing you asked for — one interactive page, not five markdown files. Pushed to PR #20.

## What''s on it

| Section | What it does |
|---|---|
| **The loop, in one picture** | Your actual cycle drawn out — engineered prompt → report → *"help me visualize this"* → dashboard, with the return arc marked "×3, no exit test" |
| **Five patterns** | Click any one → the evidence below filters to just its notes |
| **Stall points → fix** | 5 rows, 3 flagged **Act now** |
| **19 notes** | Filter by Process/Content and by source C1–C5; expand for body, source, confidence, gap |
| **9 gaps** | Severity-striped, with what closes each |
| **Handoff card** | Plus the Phase P prompt with a copy button |

## Red-team pass — what I changed

| Failed | Fixed |
|---|---|
| Deliverable wasn''t an artifact | Rebuilt as one; markdown kept as the source of record |
| Diagram was described, not drawn | The loop is now the first thing you see |
| Traceability was a claim you''d have to verify by reading | Now a click: pattern → its notes |
| Verdict buried in a file | Partial-pass chip in the header, with the 5-of-50 shortfall next to it |

**Unchanged and deliberate:** still 5 conversations. The artifact makes the shortfall more visible, not less.

**Next:** add a diverse batch (non-health, older) and re-run — or run Phase P fresh from the copy button. Round 2 spent. **PASSES.**');
