ch | ChatGPT | 2025-10-14 → 17 | **Legal** | \"Living Notebook\" RLN capture → Affidavit B → 4 court-ready PDFs → **CNN (\"Convolutional Narrative\") Map v2 → v3** of the litigation. Exhibit C PDF offered, not delivered. |\n| **C7** | ChatGPT 13 — financial & legal hardship | ChatGPT | 2025-10-14 → 17 | **Legal / financial** | Affidavit → RLN master node + damages ledger ($693,000 across 8 lines) + medical risk timeline → 5 packet templates → 5 PDFs. **Five consecutive confirmation-request turns before the first document.** Promised markdown versions never delivered. |\n| **C8** | ChatGPT 7 — academic retaliation cascade | ChatGPT | 2025-10-14 → 17 | **Legal** | RLN node scored 90/100 severity → Statement of Causal Harm → PDF → appendices PDF. **Ends with the same question asked three times in a row; four promised documents never produced.** |\n\n**What Round 2 added:** a second platform (ChatGPT), a second domain (legal/financial), and a second point in time (Oct 2025, ~5 months before C1–C5). This is what makes cross-checking possible for the first time — a pattern present on both platforms and in both domains is far more likely to be *his* than one model''s habit.\n\n## Also present — reference files, NOT conversations\n\n| ID | File | What it is | Why it is outside the corpus |\n|----|------|-----------|------------------------------|\n| **R1** | `examples.md` | Prompt-optimization before/after reference, 10 worked examples across platforms | No dialogue, no ask→outcome sequence. Matches the `prompt-optimizer` skill in his workspace; authorship unknown — may be third-party skill content. |\n| **R2** | `cybertruck_domain_knowledge.md` | Factual notes: 48V architecture, jump-start voltage ranges, NYC parts availability | A distilled fact sheet, not a conversation. Evidence that he keeps structured reference files for one-off practical problems. |\n| — | `Personal_Data_Embedding_Living_AI_Guide.md` | **The BigQuery/RAG pipeline guide is attached.** Notes are formatted to drop into its `documents` schema — see `04-HANDOFF.md`. |\n\n## What is still missing (named, not filled)\n\n| Missing | Impact |\n|---------|--------|\n| **~42 of ~50 conversations** | Still a 16% sample. Better than 10%; indicative, not representative. |\n| **2021 – mid-2025** | Corpus now spans **Oct 2025 → Mar 2026 (~5 months)**. Four of the five years in the stated 2021–2026 arc are absent. |\n| **His own messages in C6–C8** | The ChatGPT exports captured **only assistant turns**. What he asked must be inferred from what the AI answered. Every C6–C8 behavioral claim is one inference-step removed. |\n| **Final deliverables in 4 of 8** | C3, C6, C7 and C8 all end with a promised artifact absent. Truncation and genuine non-delivery cannot be distinguished from the export alone. |\n| **Raw source data** | Wearable CSVs (C1–C5) and legal exhibits (C6–C8) are not in session. All reported figures are AI-stated and unverified here. |\n\n**Bottom line for scope:** the pipeline is now cross-checked across two platforms, two domains and two time points — enough to say which patterns are his rather than one model''s. Still not enough to characterize 2021–2026.\n", "file_path": "/home/user/claude-/agentic-memory/field-test-01/00-INVENTORY.md"}');
