23	## Stage 1: Data Extraction from All Sources
24	
25	### Step 1.1: Authentication Setup
26	
27	Register applications and obtain credentials for each data source:
28	
29	| Source | Auth Method | Endpoint/Access | Rate Limit |
30	|--------|------------|-----------------|------------|
31	| Google Drive | OAuth 2.0 (`drive.readonly` scope) | `GET https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files` | 1,000,000 units/min/project |
32	| Gmail | OAuth 2.0 (`gmail.readonly` scope) | `GET https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/{userId}/messages` | 250 units/user/sec |
33	| Notion | Integration Token (Bearer) | `GET https://api.notion.com/v1/blocks/{block_id}/children` | 3 requests/sec |
34	| Twitter/X | OAuth 2.0 or Data Archive | `GET /2/users/{id}/tweets` | 1500 req/15 min |
35	| Reddit | OAuth 2.0 | `GET /user/{username}/history` | 100 queries/min |
36	| Telegram | TDLib or Desktop Export | In-app "Export Telegram Data" | N/A (local) |
37	| Discord | Bot Token (NOT user token) | `GET /channels/{channel.id}/messages` | 50 req/sec |
38	| iCloud | Privacy data dump | https://privacy.apple.com | N/A (manual) |
39	
40	### Step 1.2: Google Drive Extraction
41	
42	```python
43	import subprocess, json
44	
45	def list_folder(folder_id):
46	    params = json.dumps({
47	        "q": f"''{folder_id}'' in parents and trashed = false",
48	        "fields": "files(id,name,mimeType,size,modifiedTime)",
49	        "pageSize": 1000
50	    })
51	    cmd = ["gws", "drive", "files", "list", "--params", params]
52	    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
53	    return json.loads(result.stdout).get("files", [])
54	
55	# For Google Docs → export as plain text:
56	# gws drive files export --params ''{"fileId": "ID", "mimeType": "text/plain"}'' -o filename.txt
57	
58	# For binary files (PDF, DOCX) → download directly:
59	# gws drive files get --params ''{"fileId": "ID", "alt": "media"}'' -o filename.pdf
60	```
61	
62	### Step 1.3: Gmail Extraction
63	
64	```python
65	# List all messages
66	# GET https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/messages?maxResults=500
67	
68	# Fetch full message (RFC822 format for complete content)
69	# GET https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/messages/{id}?format=raw
70	
71	# Parse with Python''s email module:
72	import base64, email
73	raw_msg = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(response[''raw''])
74	msg = email.message_from_bytes(raw_msg)
75	```
