115	
116	## Stage 2: BigQuery Format Requirements
117	
118	### The Exact URL Format BigQuery Requires
119	
120	BigQuery loads data **exclusively from Google Cloud Storage** using `gs://` URIs:
121	
122	```
123	gs://<bucket_name>/<object_path>
124	```
125	
126	**Examples:**
127	```
128	gs://my-personal-data-bucket/knowledge_base/2024/notes.jsonl
129	gs://my-personal-data-bucket/embeddings/chunk_*.jsonl
130	gs://my-personal-data-bucket/exports/gmail_archive.avro
131	```
132	
133	### Step 2.1: Supported Formats (Ranked by Performance)
134	
135	| Format | Extension | Best For | Notes |
136	|--------|-----------|----------|-------|
137	| **Avro** | `.avro` | Best overall performance | Self-describing schema, preferred by Google |
138	| **Parquet** | `.parquet` | Columnar analytics | Excellent compression, fast queries |
139	| **JSONL** | `.jsonl` | Flexible nested data | Must be newline-delimited (NOT regular JSON) |
140	| **CSV** | `.csv` | Simple tabular data | Must be UTF-8, no nested fields |
141	| **ORC** | `.orc` | Hadoop ecosystem | Good compression |
142	
143	### Step 2.2: The Exact JSON Schema for Personal Knowledge Base
144	
145	```json
146	[
147	  {
148	    "name": "document_id",
149	    "type": "STRING",
150	    "mode": "REQUIRED"
151	  },
152	  {
153	    "name": "title",
154	    "type": "STRING",
155	    "mode": "NULLABLE"
156	  },
157	  {
158	    "name": "content",
159	    "type": "STRING",
160	    "mode": "NULLABLE"
161	  },
162	  {
163	    "name": "source_type",
164	    "type": "STRING",
165	    "mode": "REQUIRED",
166	    "description": "email | note | pdf | chat | social | browser"
167	  },
168	  {
169	    "name": "life_domain",
170	    "type": "STRING",
171	    "mode": "NULLABLE",
172	    "description": "career | finance | health | learning | personal | creative | relationships | home | digital | reference"
173	  },
174	  {
175	    "name": "metadata",
176	    "type": "RECORD",
177	    "mode": "NULLABLE",
178	    "fields": [
179	      {"name": "source", "type": "STRING", "mode": "NULLABLE"},
180	      {"name": "author", "type": "STRING", "mode": "NULLABLE"},
181	      {"name": "created_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP", "mode": "NULLABLE"},
182	      {"name": "modified_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP", "mode": "NULLABLE"},
183	      {"name": "tags", "type": "STRING", "mode": "REPEATED"},
184	      {"name": "importance_score", "type": "FLOAT", "mode": "NULLABLE"},
185	      {"name": "triage_category", "type": "STRING", "mode": "NULLABLE"}
186	    ]
187	  },
188	  {
189	    "name": "embeddings",
190	    "type": "FLOAT",
191	    "mode": "REPEATED",
192	    "description": "Vector embeddings array (768-3072 dimensions)"
193	  },
194	  {
195	    "name": "chunk_index",
196	    "type": "INTEGER",
197	    "mode": "NULLABLE"
198	  },
199	  {
200	    "name": "ingestion_timestamp",
201	    "type": "TIMESTAMP",
202	    "mode": "REQUIRED"
203	  }
204	]
205	```
206	
207	### Step 2.3: The Exact `bq load` Command
208	
209	```bash
210	# Upload data to GCS first
211	gsutil cp ./knowledge_base_export.jsonl gs://my-personal-data-bucket/knowledge_base/
212	
213	# Load into BigQuery with partitioning
214	bq --location=US load \
215	  --source_format=NEWLINE_DELIMITED_JSON \
216	  --time_partitioning_type=MONTH \
217	  --time_partitioning_field=ingestion_timestamp \
218	  --clustering_fields=source_type,life_domain \
219	  --autodetect \
220	  myproject:personal_kb.documents \
221	  gs://my-personal-data-bucket/knowledge_base/knowledge_base_export.jsonl \
222	  ./schema.json
223	```
224	
225	### Step 2.4: Critical BigQuery Constraints
226	
227	- **URI format**: Must use `gs://` prefix. No double slashes after bucket name.
228	- **JSONL only**: Regular JSON arrays are NOT supported. Each line = one record.
229	- **Nested depth**: Maximum 15 levels of `RECORD` types.
230	- **Export limit**: `files.export` capped at 10 MB per file.
231	- **Partitions**: Maximum 4,000 partitions per table.
232	- **Wildcards**: `gs://bucket/data/*.jsonl` supported, but only one `*` per path.
233	- **IAM**: Requires `roles/bigquery.dataEditor` + `roles/storage.admin`.
234	
