238	
239	### Step 3.1: Domain Taxonomy
240	
241	| Domain | Description | Example Content | Triage Priority |
242	|--------|-------------|-----------------|-----------------|
243	| Career & Work | Professional life | Contracts, CVs, schedules | HIGH |
244	| Finance & Legal | Legal cases, financial records | Court filings, tax docs | CRITICAL |
245	| Health & Wellness | Medical records | FMLA docs, prescriptions | CRITICAL |
246	| Learning & Education | Courses, credentials | Certifications, papers | STANDARD |
247	| Personal & Identity | Immigration, identity | Visa docs, personal statements | HIGH |
248	| Creative & Projects | Side projects | Business plans, writing | STANDARD |
249	| Relationships & Social | Communications | Messages, testimonies | STANDARD |
250	| Home & Logistics | Housing, vehicles | Leases, insurance | HIGH |
251	| Digital & Technical | Tech, AI tools | ChatGPT exports, configs | REFERENCE |
252	| Reference & Archive | Saved materials | Policies, guides | ARCHIVE |
253	
254	### Step 3.2: Automated Classification Pipeline
255	
256	Use the parallel analysis approach from the Life Intelligence Engine:
257	
258	```python
259	# Segment files into batches of 50
260	# For each segment, run 6-layer analysis:
261	# Layer 1: Content Inventory (what is this file?)
262	# Layer 2: Domain Classification (which life domain?)
263	# Layer 3: Entity Extraction (people, orgs, dates, amounts)
264	# Layer 4: Key Themes & Patterns
265	# Layer 5: Importance & Urgency Triage (score 1-10)
266	# Layer 6: Cross-Reference Signals (connections between docs)
267	
268	# Output per document:
269	{
270	  "document_id": "uuid",
271	  "primary_domain": "finance_legal",
272	  "secondary_domains": ["career_work"],
273	  "importance_score": 8.5,
274	  "triage_category": "CRITICAL-LEGAL",
275	  "key_entities": ["IRS", "2024 Tax Return", "$45,000"],
276	  "cross_references": ["doc_uuid_123", "doc_uuid_456"]
277	}
