282	## Stage 4: Vector Embedding Generation
283	
284	### Step 4.1: Choose Your Embedding Model
285	
286	| Model | Dimensions | Token Limit | Cost/1M Tokens | Best For |
287	|-------|-----------|-------------|----------------|----------|
288	| OpenAI `text-embedding-3-large` | 3072 | 8,191 | $0.13 | General purpose, highest quality |
289	| Cohere `embed-v3` | 1024 | 512 | $0.10 | Cheapest, multilingual |
290	| Google `text-embedding-004` | 768 | 2,048 | $0.15 | Google ecosystem integration |
291	| Voyage AI `voyage-3-large` | 1024 | 32,000 | $0.18 | Longest context, best for docs |
292	
293	### Step 4.2: Chunking Strategy
294	
295	**Recommended: Recursive chunking with semantic boundaries**
296	
297	```python
298	from langchain.text_splitter import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter
299	
300	splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(
301	    chunk_size=512,           # tokens
302	    chunk_overlap=50,         # 10% overlap
303	    separators=["\n\n", "\n", ". ", " "],  # hierarchical splits
304	    length_function=len
305	)
306	
307	chunks = splitter.split_text(document_text)
308	```
309	
310	### Step 4.3: Generate Embeddings
311	
312	```python
313	import openai
314	
315	client = openai.OpenAI()
316	
317	def embed_chunks(chunks):
318	    response = client.embeddings.create(
319	        model="text-embedding-3-large",
320	        input=chunks  # batch up to 2048 chunks per call
321	    )
322	    return [item.embedding for item in response.data]
323	```
324	
325	### Step 4.4: Metadata Schema for Each Chunk
326	
327	```json
328	{
329	  "source_id": "uuid-string",
330	  "source_type": "email | note | pdf | chat | social",
331	  "author": "string",
332	  "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
333	  "life_domain": "career_work",
334	  "tags": ["meeting", "project-alpha"],
335	  "chunk_index": 3,
336	  "importance_score": 7.5,
337	  "access_level": "private"
338	}
339	```
