343	## Stage 5: Platform-Specific Injection
344	
345	### 5A: Claude Projects (Anthropic)
346	
347	**The concept**: Upload files to a Claude Project. Claude references them on every conversation turn within that project. The AI "lives in" those files.
348	
349	**Limits**: 30 MB/file (UI), 500 MB/file (API). 200K context window total.
350	
351	**Supported formats**: PDF, DOCX, CSV, TXT, HTML, JSON, XLSX, EPUB, RTF, images (JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP)
352	
353	```bash
354	# Step 1: Upload file via Files API (beta)
355	curl -X POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/files \
356	  -H "x-api-key: $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" \
357	  -H "anthropic-beta: files-api-2025-04-14" \
358	  -F "file=@/path/to/knowledge_base.pdf"
359	
360	# Response: {"id": "file_011CNha8iCJcU1wXNR6q4V8w", ...}
361	
362	# Step 2: Reference in conversation
363	curl -X POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages \
364	  -H "x-api-key: $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" \
365	  -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \
366	  -H "anthropic-beta: files-api-2025-04-14" \
367	  -d ''{
368	    "model": "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
369	    "messages": [{
370	      "role": "user",
371	      "content": [{
372	        "type": "document",
373	        "source": {"type": "file", "file_id": "file_011CNha8iCJcU1wXNR6q4V8w"}
374	      }, {
375	        "type": "text",
376	        "text": "Based on my knowledge base, what should I prioritize this week?"
377	      }]
378	    }]
379	  }''
380	```
381	
382	### 5B: Gemini Gems & NotebookLM (Google)
383	
384	**The concept**: Upload documents to NotebookLM (up to 50 sources per notebook) or create a custom Gem with persistent instructions and grounding documents.
385	
386	**Limits**: 500,000 words or 500 MB per source. 2 GB per file via API. 50 sources per notebook.
387	
388	**Supported formats**: PDF, Google Docs, TXT, CSV, Markdown, MP4, MP3, WAV, images
389	
390	```python
391	# Step 1: Upload to Google Cloud Storage for persistence
392	# (Files via standard Gemini File API expire after 48 hours)
393	gsutil cp knowledge_base.pdf gs://my-gemini-bucket/docs/
394	
395	# Step 2: Grant Gemini API access to your bucket
396	# Grant "Storage Object Viewer" role to:
397	# generativelanguage.googleapis.com service agent
398	
399	# Step 3: Reference GCS URI in Gemini API call
400	import google.generativeai as genai
401	
402	genai.configure(api_key=os.environ["GEMINI_API_KEY"])
403	model = genai.GenerativeModel("gemini-2.5-flash")
404	
405	# Upload file (temporary - 48hr expiry)
406	uploaded = genai.upload_file("knowledge_base.pdf")
407	
408	# Or reference GCS URI (persistent)
409	response = model.generate_content([
410	    {"file_data": {"file_uri": "gs://my-gemini-bucket/docs/knowledge_base.pdf", "mime_type": "application/pdf"}},
411	    "Based on my knowledge base, what should I prioritize?"
412	])
413	```
414	
415	### 5C: Microsoft Copilot Enterprise (Graph Connectors)
416	
417	**The concept**: Feed external data into Microsoft Graph via custom Graph Connectors. The Semantic Index vectorizes everything. Copilot then reasons over it using RAG — "the AI lives in the file."
418	
419	**Limits**: 512 MB per file for semantic indexing. Requires Microsoft 365 E3/E5 + Copilot license.
420	
421	```bash
422	# Step 1: Register app in Microsoft Entra admin center
423	# Grant: ExternalConnection.ReadWrite.All, ExternalItem.ReadWrite.All
424	
425	# Step 2: Create external connection
426	curl -X POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/external/connections \
427	  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" \
428	  -d ''{
429	    "id": "personalKnowledgeBase",
430	    "name": "Personal Knowledge Base",
431	    "description": "My triaged personal data"
432	  }''
433	
434	# Step 3: Define schema with semantic labels
435	curl -X PATCH https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/external/connections/personalKnowledgeBase/schema \
436	  -d ''{
437	    "baseType": "microsoft.graph.externalItem",
438	    "properties": [
439	      {"name": "title", "type": "String", "isSearchable": true, "isRetrievable": true, "labels": ["title"]},
