INSERT INTO blocks (block_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, seq, role, kind, chars, tool_name, tool_use_id, is_error, redacted, signature_sha256, signature_len, privacy_zone, zone_reason, zone_match, text) VALUES (200, '1f7532c4-100a-42bc-a21c-b2bcbc7b21ea', 154, 0, 'assistant', 'text', 2465, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Private work', 'session-internal', '', '**Artifact:** https://claude.ai/code/artifact/2a2b2fe6-6cff-4d64-a871-c6aaaf3a9550 · PDF + JSONL attached · pushed

Two of the three predicted next steps are now **done, not forecast.** The third needs exports only you can produce.

| Prediction | Status |
|---|---|
| Scale to all ~50 | **Blocked on your exports** — prompt is ready to paste |
| Score & triage the map | **Done** — in the pattern cards |
| Make the notes queryable | **Done to the credential line** |

## Triage layer

Every pattern now carries **counts, observed cost, band, fix** — and the patterns are ordered by cost, not by how interesting they are.

| Band | Patterns |
|---|---|
| **Act now** | P6 ask-then-wait · P3 render step · P1 no stop rule |
| Monitor | P8 re-priming · P5 metric fragility · P2 shorthand |
| Note only | P4 scaffolding · P7 scoring — *these are the strengths* |

Counts and bands only — no invented decimals, per your own boundary (N31). I also flagged where P1 and P6 share the same four undelivered documents, so the cost isn''t double-counted.

## The notes are queryable now

`notes.jsonl` — **34 rows, validation PASS, zero orphan claims**, against the guide''s exact `documents` schema.

Ask *"Where does my approach stall?"* in the artifact and it returns N25, N28, N27, N02, N26, N06 — every stall note, with its source conversation. **That''s the mission''s done-when, satisfied before any cloud spend.**

Three decisions worth knowing:

- **Provenance rides inside `content`** — body + source + confidence + gap. A retrieved chunk can never become an orphan claim.
- **`embeddings` is empty by design.** That''s the guide''s Stage 4, a separate step with a separate cost.
- **`build_jsonl.py` regenerates from the markdown**, so the notes stay the single source of truth — no hand-maintained copy to drift.

## What''s blocked, and one call for you

**Four steps need your Google Cloud credentials:** bucket + dataset, IAM roles, `gsutil cp` then `bq load`, then embeddings. All four are written out in `06-INGEST.md` — listed, not skipped. Once credentials exist the whole chain becomes one scheduled job.

**One judgment I flagged rather than decided:** 24 of 34 notes landed in `life_domain: digital`, which is correct by the guide''s taxonomy (process notes = AI tooling) but means querying "how I think" looks like a technical query. If you''d rather they sat under `personal`, it''s a one-line change — but it changes every future query, so it''s yours to call.');
