INSERT INTO blocks (block_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, seq, role, kind, chars, tool_name, tool_use_id, is_error, redacted, signature_sha256, signature_len, privacy_zone, zone_reason, zone_match, text) VALUES (206, 'a9f80bde-62eb-4bf1-959a-b7260e11ccea', 158, 1, 'assistant', 'text', 1945, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Confidential', 'medical', 'prescription', 'Two things I can do without anything from you. Four need you. And one correction that changes the ranking.

## Correction first

The artifact says *"this repository is that fix"* for the re-priming pattern (P8). **It isn''t yet.** I just checked — there''s no `CLAUDE.md` or standing-instructions file in the repo. It holds the *outputs*, not the operating rules. So P8''s fix is still a claim, not a file.

That makes it the top item.

## What I can do now

| # | Move | Why it''s first |
|---|---|---|
| **1** | **Write LOOP OS into the repo** as `CLAUDE.md` | Turns P8''s fix real, and encodes the other four fixes as rules: propose-then-confirm (P6), report **+** artefact by default (P3), the shorthand glossary (P2), "inputs present: X/Y" (P5). The map''s own prescription, applied. Every future session in this repo loads it — no re-priming. |
| 2 | **Verify the health citations** (N15–N18) | Closes G5. Scite and Elicit are connected, so I can check the PMIDs and trials myself. This is the gap your own loop never touches (N07) — worth having done for you. |

## What needs you

| Move | Cost to you |
|---|---|
| **Re-export C6–C8 with your messages** (G10) | Minutes. Upgrades 3 of 8 conversations from inference to direct evidence. |
| Export the rest, **oldest first** (G1, G2) | The five-year arc is still missing four years. |
| **Google Cloud credentials** → load the JSONL, then embed | Four steps, listed in `06-INGEST.md`. |
| **`digital` vs `personal`** for the 24 process notes | One-line change, but it shapes every future query. |

Also open: **PR #20** — docs-only, no CI, no review comments. Merge whenever.

## My recommendation

**Do #1 now.** It''s the only item that makes every future session cheaper, it needs nothing from you, and the field test''s whole finding was that your loop lives in chat windows instead of in files. Fixing that in the repo is the thing this exercise was actually for.

Say go and I''ll write it.');
