INSERT INTO tool_calls (tool_use_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, name, input_json, result_chars, is_error) VALUES ('toolu_01VJcGSdube1c5aGjkd6UrcM', '2e18eb86-24c6-43d8-9950-b67e29eea513', 46, 'Bash', '{"command": "git add agentic-memory/field-test-01/field-test-01.html && git commit -q -F - <<''EOF'' && git log --oneline -1\nAdd interactive artifact for Phase R field test deliverable\n\nRenders the inventory, 19 atomic notes, pattern map, gap list and\nhandoff card as a single self-contained page: a loop diagram of the\nobserved ask-report-visualize cycle, pattern cards that filter the\nsupporting evidence, and note filters by type and source. Theme-aware,\nno external assets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9d28RssdrvJVAzTpi2doW\nEOF", "description": "Commit the artifact HTML"}', 67, 0);
INSERT INTO tool_calls (tool_use_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, name, input_json, result_chars, is_error) VALUES ('toolu_01HkfhkF9oSNGKdmQVDRKuDv', '677f8019-4f4a-4ecf-90e2-773d97b79673', 48, 'Bash', '{"command": "for i in 1 2 3 4; do git push -u origin claude/agentic-memory-field-test-q6uhce && echo PUSH_OK && break; s=$((2**i)); echo \"retry in ${s}s\"; sleep $s; done", "description": "Push branch with retries"}', 277, 0);
INSERT INTO tool_calls (tool_use_id, turn_uuid, turn_no, name, input_json, result_chars, is_error) VALUES ('toolu_0134nPNVCtDDEfRA2rrvhDtJ', '0c78aca2-2c46-4758-a43d-fc462f3d10c1', 52, 'Write', '{"content": "# Phase R — Inventory (Field Test #1, Round 2)\n\n**Rule followed:** work only on what exists; name what is missing; no claims about unseen data.\n\n## Conversation corpus — 8 of ~50\n\n| ID | Conversation | Platform | Conversation date | Domain | What it is |\n|----|--------------|----------|-------------------|--------|------------|\n| **C1** | Building RNN and CNN with audiovisuals | Claude | ~Feb–Mar 2026 | Health / meta-system | Meal decode folded into a \"Biological AI Second Brain\" (CNN→RNN→RL). \"Perfect output / red-team\" prompt re-issued 3×; output rebuilt prose → dashboard → dashboard on real wearable data. |\n| **C2** | Long COVID dysautonomia with Brugada analysis | Claude | ~Mar 2026 | Health | Engineered master-prompt → 9-section clinical report. Loop Score 6.7. Then \"Help me visualize this data\" → 5-tab dashboard. |\n| **C3** | Cost-effective compression wraps | Claude | ~Mar 2026 | Health | POTS compression prompt. AI asks 3 clarifying questions; he removes two constraints and hands the third back. **Deliverable absent — truncated at research launch.** |\n| **C4** | Autonomic intelligence report, medication nonadherence | Claude | ~Mar 2026 | Health | Master-prompt **v2.0 (Red-Team Validated)** — refinement of C2. Same patient/data/formula. Loop Score 5.7. Then \"Help me visualize this data\". |\n| **C5** | Long COVID autonomic management synthesis | Claude | ~Mar 2026 | Health | 80+ source literature synthesis with credibility tags. Then \"Help me visualize this data\" → 6-tab dashboard. |\n| **C6** | ChatGPT 16 — HR retaliation & privacy breach | ChatGPT | 2025-10-14 → 17 | **Legal** | \"Living Notebook\" RLN capture → Affidavit B → 4 court-ready PDFs → **CNN (\"Convolutional Narrative\") Map v2 → v3** of the litigation. Exhibit C PDF offered, not delivered. |\n| **C7** | ChatGPT 13 — financial & legal hardship | ChatGPT | 2025-10-14 → 17 | **Legal / financial** | Affidavit → RLN master node + damages ledger ($693,000 across 8 lines) + medical risk timeline → 5 packet templates → 5 PDFs. **Five consecutive confirmation-request turns before the first document.** Promised markdown versions not delivered. |\n| **C8** | ChatGPT 7 — academic retaliation cascade | ChatGPT | 2025-10-14 → 17 | **Legal** | RLN node with a severity score of 90/100 → Statement of Causal Harm → PDF → appendices PDF. **Ends with the same question asked three times in a row; four promised documents never produced.** |\n\n**What Round 2 added:** a second platform (ChatGPT), a second domain (legal/financial), and a second point in time (Oct 2025, ~5 months before C1–C5). This is what makes cross-checking possible for the first time.\n\n## Also present — reference files, NOT conversations\n\n| ID | File | What it is | Why it is excluded from the corpus |\n|----|------|-----------|-----------------------------------|\n| **R1** | `examples.md` | Prompt-optimization before/after reference, 10 worked examples across platforms | No dialogue, no ask→outcome sequence. Matches the `prompt-optimizer` skill in his workspace; authorship unknown — may be third-party skill content. |\n| **R2** | `cybertruck_domain_knowledge.md` | Factual notes: 48V architecture, jump-start voltages, NYC parts availability | A distilled fact sheet, not a conversation. Shows he keeps structured reference files for one-off practical problems. |\n| — | `Personal_Data_Embedding_Living_AI_Guide.md` | **The BigQuery/RAG pipeline guide is attached.** Notes are formatted to drop into its `documents` schema (see `04-HANDOFF.md`). |\n\n## What is still missing (named, not filled)\n\n| Missing | Impact |\n|---------|--------|\n| **~42 of ~50 conversations** | Still a 16% sample. Better than 10%, still indicative rather than representative. |\n| **2021 – mid-2025** | Corpus now spans **Oct 2025 → Mar 2026 (~5 months)**. The earlier four years of the stated 2021–2026 arc are absent. |\n| **His own messages in C6–C8** | The ChatGPT exports captured **only assistant turns**. What he asked must be inferred from what the AI answered. Every C6–C8 behavioral claim is one inference-step removed. |\n| **Final deliverables in 4 of 8** | C3, C6, C7, C8 all end with a promised artifact absent. Truncation and genuine non-delivery cannot be distinguished. |\n| **Raw source data** | Wearable CSVs (C1–C5) and legal exhibits (C6–C8) are not in session. Reported figures are AI-stated, unverified here. |\n\n**Bottom line for scope:** the pipeline is now cross-checked on two platforms, two domains and two time points — enough to say which patterns are *his* rather than one model''s habits. Still not enough to characterize 2021–2026.\n", "file_path": "/home/user/claude-/agentic-memory/field-test-01/00-INVENTORY.md"}', 96, 1);
